; spec/assets/geneva12.art -- InitechOS "Geneva 12" application-font strike,
; the LOCKED hand-authored source (bead initech-uelk). Rule 8: this file is
; the contract; spec/assets/geneva12.h is GENERATED from it by
; tools/geneva12_art2h.c (make gen-geneva12; test-geneva12-art proves the
; committed header is byte-identical to a fresh transcription).
;
; WHY: Mac OS 8.1 SimpleText draws its document in Geneva 12 (16-px lines),
; ../system7-decomp specs/sys8/simpletext-stdfile.md Sec 1.2 [MEAS] (mint-007)
; (Font menu check on Geneva, Size menu check on 12 Point; line pitch 16;
; "Saving " 45 px, "tables" 39 px, "PC LOAD LETTER" 101 px). InitechText
; (TEXT.EXE) drew Geneva 9 because no Geneva 12 strike existed here.
;
; PROVENANCE (Law 1 honesty) -- two different kinds of data live here:
;   METRICS (the "lb"/"aw" numbers on every glyph line) are MEASUREMENTS of the
;     real Mac OS 8.1 Geneva 12 strike: NFNT 12112 of the "Geneva" suitcase
;     (FOND 3, FAT entry size 12 style 0 -> NFNT 12112) in System Folder:Fonts
;     of ../system7-decomp goldens/work/boot81.img, extracted to
;     ../system7-decomp mint/work/geneva12/NFNT_12112.bin (md5
;     3e289fee44b6f1b9b89ac5343647ef2b; mint/work/geneva12/mint-results-011.md).
;     owTable: high byte = left bearing lb, low byte = advance aw (font-
;     manager.md Sec 1.1); FontRec ascent 12, descent 3, leading 1, widMax 15,
;     fRectHeight 15. The missing-glyph line carries the owTable missing entry
;     (index lastChar+1 = 0xDA: lb 0, aw 10). Copied mechanically from the
;     owTable bytes by a scratch script. Functional metrics are citable
;     (geneva.md "Clean-room boundary").
;   GLYPH ART (the '#' maps) is HAND-AUTHORED for this file to the Geneva
;     typeface DESIGN (1-px stems, cap height 9 rows = rows 3..11 as measured
;     in the SimpleText capture, simpletext-stdfile.md Sec 1.2 "line 1 caps
;     y=47..55", descenders rows 12..14, "'g' rows y=56..58"). It was NOT
;     transcribed, traced or copied from the real strike bitmap (Apple IP,
;     reference-only; geneva.md "Clean-room boundary", PRD Sec 6.4 / Sec 12).
;     The NFNT locationTable glyph-image WIDTHS (extents only, no pixel data)
;     sized each ink box. After the first draft the real strike was used AS A
;     DIFF ORACLE on per-glyph ink BOUNDING BOXES only (the chicago12.art
;     process): it flagged " # ' * - / = @ \ _ p q | and the missing box, which
;     were then REDRAWN by hand to the corrected extents (no pixel was copied).
;     test-geneva12-metrics re-runs that bbox comparison against the resource
;     on every run.
;
; FORMAT: one block per glyph, codes 0x20..0x7E in order, then "missing".
;   glyph <code|missing> lb <n> aw <n>
;   16 rows, each exactly aw characters: '#' = ink, '.' = paper. Row 12 is the
;   first row below the baseline (ascent 12); row 15 is the leading row and is
;   always blank. The cell is the advance: the renderer paints exactly aw
;   columns. The leftmost ink column of every inked printable glyph MUST equal
;   lb (the transcriber fails loud otherwise); the missing box may start right
;   of lb (its NFNT image carries a blank first column). No ink at or beyond aw.
; ASCII-clean (Rule 12). Lines starting ';' are comments.
